From c94eb12d3d8436f8c11ec4cc9dd6ce3ee9759a59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: G1 repro <repro@localhost>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 15:23:57 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] G1 vendor: changes of the vendor zephyr tree

The shipped v1.66 image was built from a private, modified zephyr commit
(833f89df...-dirty, not in sdk-zephyr).  These are its differences from
sdk-zephyr v3.4.99-ncs1-1 as far as they show in the image.  Replaced lines
become comments, not deletions, where the line numbers of the asserts after
them must not move.

subsys/bluetooth/host/hci_core.c (1.66; not in 1.63)
- bt_hci_cmd_send_sync_timeout(): a copy of bt_hci_cmd_send_sync() with a
  timeout in milliseconds and an assert_on_timeout flag; without the flag a
  timeout logs "command opcode 0x%04x timeout with err %d" and returns
  -ETIMEDOUT.  It follows bt_hci_cmd_send_sync() in .text and is 59 lines
  long with its BT_ASSERT_MSG on line 390; one line is added before
  bt_hci_cmd_create() (its __ASSERT_NO_MSG moved from 266 to 267, the
  send_sync assert from 338 to 339, every later assert by 61).  The fifth
  k_sem_init() caller in the file makes GCC emit k_sem_init out of line
  (a b.w to z_impl_k_sem_init), which changes the scheduling around the
  other four calls (bt_init, bt_enable).  The prototype is in hci.h for
  the application, which calls it from the ANCS start-up.

subsys/bluetooth/host/conn.c
- L2 is the default security level and the set_security early return is
  disabled.
- Three compiled-out LOG_DBG lines are gone: "no controller bufs" in
  send_frag() (replaced by a comment, which keeps send_frag's register
  allocation and the line numbers), "Adding conn %p to poll list" in
  conn_prepare_events() and LOG_DBG("") in bt_conn_prepare_events() (deleted,
  which moves the assert line numbers of every later function by two).
  Every zephyr version with this code has the lines.  Firmware 1.45 to 1.56
  match a conn.c with only the two security changes above; 1.63 and 1.66
  match this one, so the vendor removed the three lines together.

drivers/flash/nrf_qspi_nor.c
- Stock in 1.66 (and 1.45 to 1.56): the DK flash timings in the devicetree
  (t-enter-dpd 10000, t-exit-dpd 35000) give the k_busy_wait blocks of
  enter_dpd()/exit_dpd().  Only firmware 1.63 had a printk marker in
  enter_dpd() and no busy-wait blocks.

The lsm6dso, dmic and lib/crc changes below and the security changes in
conn.c are in all firmware versions from 1.45 to 1.66.

drivers/sensor/lsm6dso/lsm6dso.c
- The driver logs through printk, at log level DBG.
- The device has no init function: the application calls lsm6dso_init(),
  which is exported, does not print "Initialize device" and returns 0 when
  the chip does not answer.

drivers/audio/dmic_nrfx_pdm.c
- Default gain 0x40 on both channels.

lib/crc/CMakeLists.txt
- crc8_sw.c is not part of libzephyr: the vendor application compiles it as
  its own source.  The image has a single crc8_ccitt, used by NVS too, at the
  end of the application code.  NVS forces CONFIG_CRC on and libzephyr is
  linked whole, so the file cannot be in both.
---
 drivers/audio/dmic_nrfx_pdm.c    |  1 +
 drivers/sensor/lsm6dso/lsm6dso.c | 94 ++++++++++++++++----------------
 include/zephyr/bluetooth/hci.h   |  6 ++
 lib/crc/CMakeLists.txt           |  3 +-
 subsys/bluetooth/host/conn.c     | 14 ++---
 subsys/bluetooth/host/hci_core.c | 61 +++++++++++++++++++++
 6 files changed, 123 insertions(+), 56 deletions(-)

